 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? Most of them do. They keep the table for several minutes after you leave, so you' never stuck outside during their busy hour. Most places are good about moving you inside, even if there's a standby table. It never hurts to call and ask. Most places won't charge you if you cancel within reason. If you call more than an hour before, they'll usually keep the table for you. Okay, no worries. Just always check the small print on emails you rarely open. You' be surprised what's in them.",
